# Build context exclusions for images built from the REPO ROOT
# (currently apps/worker/Dockerfile — see render.yaml's dockerContext: .).
#
# The sidecar builds from services/docling-sidecar and uses its own
# .dockerignore; this file does not apply there.
#
# The .env rules are the important ones and are a security control, not an
# optimisation. The worker Dockerfile does `COPY packages ./packages` and
# `COPY apps/worker ./apps/worker`, both of which would otherwise bake real
# secrets — the Neon password, Gemini, Clerk, R2 and Resend keys — into an image
# layer, where they survive in the published image whether or not a later layer
# deletes them. Secrets reach the container through Render's environment, never
# through the build context.
#
# ".env.example" is deliberately NOT excluded: the pattern matches the exact
# name ".env", and shipping the documented template costs nothing.

**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Installed inside the image by `bun install`. Copying the host's copy would be
# slower and platform-wrong — native binaries built for Windows/macOS do not run
# on the linux image.
**/node_modules

# Built inside the image. Excluding the host's output prevents a stale local
# build from silently shadowing the real one.
**/dist
**/.output

# Local caches and run artefacts.
**/.turbo
**/.runs
**/*.log
.vercel

# Not needed by the worker image.
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
services
apps/web/src
apps/web/public
**/*.test.ts
